WEBVTT

00:42.542 --> 00:45.962
SOLD OUT ON YOU

00:50.508 --> 00:51.843
Mechoori!

00:53.470 --> 00:54.596
Let me sleep over.

00:55.597 --> 00:56.431
What?

00:57.390 --> 00:58.641
Let's sleep together.

01:08.651 --> 01:10.070
I can't believe it.

01:10.862 --> 01:13.323
You really packed your stuff
and came here at this hour?

01:13.406 --> 01:14.949
You said you couldn't sleep

01:15.033 --> 01:15.867
without me.

01:17.452 --> 01:19.704
I didn't mean anything by it.

01:19.788 --> 01:21.581
What about the farm?

01:21.664 --> 01:23.333
I had a lot to check before our contract,

01:23.416 --> 01:25.543
so I was going to stay in Seoul
for a bit anyway.

01:26.169 --> 01:27.170
Are you sure about this?

01:28.671 --> 01:30.423
And you? Is this okay?

01:31.090 --> 01:31.925
Should I just go?

01:32.008 --> 01:33.593
Who said it wasn't okay?

01:35.804 --> 01:37.597
Where was your room again?

01:37.680 --> 01:39.724
Mechoori, wait.

01:39.808 --> 01:40.850
Let me clean up a bit!

01:40.934 --> 01:41.768
Hang on…

02:30.108 --> 02:31.151
Come here.

03:29.667 --> 03:30.501
What are you doing?

03:31.127 --> 03:32.921
You didn't get any sleep.

03:33.963 --> 03:35.798
I'll play this for you
until you fall asleep.

03:35.882 --> 03:36.966
This is really helpful.

03:45.183 --> 03:46.726
It's fine.

03:48.144 --> 03:49.896
When are you going to sleep?

03:49.979 --> 03:52.190
I'll go sleep on the sofa
after you fall asleep.

03:52.273 --> 03:53.399
What?

03:53.483 --> 03:55.401
Why? Why the sofa?

03:55.485 --> 03:58.321
The sofa's small, and my bed's pretty big.

03:59.405 --> 04:00.240
The sofa's big too.

04:02.742 --> 04:03.576
Just sleep.

04:04.535 --> 04:06.913
My sofa's really uncomfortable,

04:06.996 --> 04:08.831
and my bed's really comfy.

04:38.278 --> 04:39.279
Hurry up and sleep.

05:02.135 --> 05:03.136
You're not saying

05:03.219 --> 05:05.096
you want to stay in Korea, are you?

05:06.889 --> 05:08.266
Is it because of that host?

05:21.904 --> 05:22.864
Ms. Dam.

05:22.947 --> 05:24.073
Mr. Seo…

05:24.991 --> 05:26.075
Oh, my neighbor.

05:26.159 --> 05:28.286
You can just keep calling me Mr. Seo.

05:28.369 --> 05:30.246
I've decided to take back my position.

05:31.080 --> 05:32.540
You know I'm rooting for you, right?

05:33.249 --> 05:34.834
You're getting me fired up already.

05:34.917 --> 05:37.253
You should eat well at a time like this.

05:37.337 --> 05:40.798
I'll send you a list
of nice restaurants in the area.

05:42.800 --> 05:43.801
Good luck!

05:46.012 --> 05:46.971
No!

06:02.862 --> 06:04.655
I'm running a lap around the park.

06:18.419 --> 06:21.714
BRAISED QUAIL EGGS, RADISH SALAD

06:35.770 --> 06:36.979
They're all so salty.

06:49.367 --> 06:52.912
Their rice was milled just yesterday,
so it should taste great.

06:55.248 --> 06:56.374
Thank you.

06:58.668 --> 07:00.044
I'm getting one too.

07:03.965 --> 07:05.007
PREMIUM-GRADE RICE

07:10.054 --> 07:12.473
These quail eggs are probably more fresh.

07:13.766 --> 07:15.560
The ones with rougher shells are better.

07:15.643 --> 07:17.186
Are you a chef?

07:18.813 --> 07:20.231
I know my way around quail eggs.

07:25.486 --> 07:26.696
Thanks.

07:27.280 --> 07:28.531
I'm getting some too.

07:29.991 --> 07:31.409
FRESH QUAIL EGGS

07:40.334 --> 07:42.003
Are you making wraps for lunch today?

07:42.086 --> 07:46.424
The side dishes at home were too salty,
so I thought making wraps would be nice.

07:46.507 --> 07:50.178
Right, they shouldn't be salty.
Everyone's into low sodium these days.

07:50.970 --> 07:51.971
Right?

07:52.597 --> 07:54.223
-Bye, then.
-Bye.

08:44.857 --> 08:46.692
So we're neighbors.

08:47.276 --> 08:48.486
Do you live alone?

08:48.569 --> 08:49.403
No.

08:50.488 --> 08:54.158
Then the person you cook for
would be really happy.

08:55.284 --> 08:56.118
You too.

09:19.934 --> 09:21.602
Was my food that salty?

09:24.313 --> 09:26.107
Was it?

09:40.329 --> 09:41.747
Ye-jin.

09:47.295 --> 09:49.130
-Will you try tasting it?
-Sure.

09:54.844 --> 09:56.721
-It's tasty.
-Is it okay?

09:57.305 --> 09:58.556
I'm glad.

10:03.144 --> 10:04.437
Were you running with Mr. Seo?

10:05.771 --> 10:08.024
We just ran into each other at the park.

10:13.321 --> 10:16.115
You're the one who helped Ye-jin, right?

10:16.198 --> 10:17.575
Executive Director Seo Eric.

10:19.035 --> 10:21.579
I wanted to treat you to a meal sometime.

10:21.662 --> 10:23.372
I'm not sure if it'll suit your taste.

10:23.456 --> 10:24.540
It already looks delicious.

10:24.624 --> 10:26.500
I can sense that you're a true pro.

10:26.584 --> 10:27.918
How did you know?

10:28.002 --> 10:30.504
I teach cooking classes
at a community center.

10:30.588 --> 10:34.175
No wonder you're so skilled
with a knife, sir.

10:35.134 --> 10:36.218
You think so?

10:41.849 --> 10:43.225
Oh, right. The onions.

10:43.309 --> 10:44.977
The onions.

10:47.647 --> 10:48.606
Onions!

10:48.689 --> 10:49.982
Here you go.

10:53.277 --> 10:56.197
Don't just stand there. Sit down.

10:56.280 --> 10:57.365
Yes, sir.

10:57.448 --> 10:59.200
You're quite clumsy, aren't you?

11:10.252 --> 11:11.128
All right.

11:11.212 --> 11:13.255
Wow, that looks amazing!

11:13.339 --> 11:14.840
This looks great, sir.

11:17.093 --> 11:18.177
Give me your plate.

11:19.678 --> 11:21.055
I can eat on my own.

11:22.264 --> 11:23.682
All right…

11:23.766 --> 11:24.892
Hand me your plate.

11:26.102 --> 11:27.186
Thank you.

11:28.270 --> 11:30.773
Here. Enjoy.

11:30.856 --> 11:31.857
If it's too salty,

11:32.566 --> 11:34.151
eat it with rice.

11:34.235 --> 11:35.820
There are veggies here too.

11:40.199 --> 11:41.867
It's not salty at all!

11:41.951 --> 11:43.869
Is this what they call
a deep, savory flavor?

11:45.204 --> 11:47.331
That's right. A savory flavor.

11:51.460 --> 11:53.129
-Hand me your plate.
-Yes, sir.

11:55.172 --> 11:56.048
I'll have a lot.

11:59.552 --> 12:00.553
Eat up.

12:00.636 --> 12:01.971
Dad, he can't eat spicy food.

12:02.054 --> 12:04.557
Ms. Dam, you must be hungry.

12:04.640 --> 12:05.850
Eat up.

12:06.559 --> 12:07.560
Wait…

12:15.401 --> 12:17.862
This is really delicious, sir.

12:18.696 --> 12:19.530
Really?

12:19.613 --> 12:21.949
-Does it suit your taste?
-Yes.

12:22.032 --> 12:23.367
The savory flavor…

12:24.243 --> 12:25.077
I'm glad.

12:26.745 --> 12:30.249
You really know how to eat, Mr. Seo.

12:30.332 --> 12:33.461
I learned that I should eat it like this.

12:33.544 --> 12:35.004
That's right.

12:35.087 --> 12:37.131
Spicy pork tastes best in a lettuce wrap.

12:52.938 --> 12:54.815
Young folks sure do have great appetites.

12:58.277 --> 12:59.153
Mechoori.

12:59.236 --> 13:01.071
Slow down.

13:02.198 --> 13:03.324
Thank you for the food.

13:03.949 --> 13:06.118
Enjoy… What…

13:06.827 --> 13:08.120
Hey, slow down.

13:08.204 --> 13:09.497
Make sure to chew properly.

13:21.926 --> 13:26.096
You're the type who only uses
low-sodium salt. Why did you eat so much?

13:27.014 --> 13:28.307
Savory taste…

13:29.558 --> 13:30.559
It was delicious.

13:34.021 --> 13:37.107
Does your father bring side dishes
for you sometimes?

13:38.108 --> 13:39.652
Not sometimes, all the time.

13:40.778 --> 13:42.947
They were all dishes
that required a lot of work.

13:43.531 --> 13:44.532
Why didn't you eat them?

13:45.699 --> 13:46.700
I know, right?

13:47.201 --> 13:49.036
The side dishes did nothing wrong.

13:49.995 --> 13:51.413
HIT HOMESHOPPING

13:52.498 --> 13:53.499
Hyun-ki,

13:54.667 --> 13:56.001
there's something I want to ask.

13:56.669 --> 13:57.586
Yes?

13:59.755 --> 14:02.216
The home shopping host Dam Ye-jin.

14:02.800 --> 14:05.135
Did she really not know
about Good Morning Cream?

14:12.977 --> 14:14.562
Dam Ye-jin

14:15.813 --> 14:18.857
was brought in at the last minute
just a week before the broadcast.

14:20.818 --> 14:21.652
What?

14:21.735 --> 14:23.153
I can guess

14:24.363 --> 14:27.783
why she jumped at the opportunity,
even when she was just a rookie.

14:30.995 --> 14:31.996
Myeong-hwa.

14:32.079 --> 14:33.622
Thirty years ago,

14:34.415 --> 14:36.500
you suddenly took a leave of absence
from school

14:37.042 --> 14:39.545
and disappeared for a whole year.

14:41.171 --> 14:42.339
There were rumors

14:42.840 --> 14:44.884
that you'd gone missing.

14:44.967 --> 14:48.178
But then I suddenly remembered
Dam Seok-gyeong,

14:48.762 --> 14:52.349
who you had dated in secret with my help.

14:53.601 --> 14:57.396
I went to the troupe that performed
the show we saw together

14:57.479 --> 14:59.899
and got his address.

15:00.900 --> 15:01.734
I went there

15:05.112 --> 15:07.197
and saw you two together.

15:07.990 --> 15:09.199
Along with your kid.

15:11.410 --> 15:13.787
When I first saw Dam Ye-jin,

15:13.871 --> 15:16.457
it was impossible not to know
she was your daughter.

15:17.333 --> 15:19.919
It was like seeing you 30 years ago.

15:22.379 --> 15:23.422
Myeong-hwa,

15:24.256 --> 15:27.676
Ye-jin was eager to do her best,

15:29.345 --> 15:31.597
because she'd be doing the broadcast
with her mother.

15:45.569 --> 15:47.029
You really used all these items?

15:48.447 --> 15:49.782
Of course.

15:49.865 --> 15:53.786
To me, this place
is like your mushroom farm.

15:53.869 --> 15:57.289
I don't allow any tricks or deceptions.

15:58.374 --> 16:01.752
I'm not someone who'd use tricks
like pressure points to make myself sweat.

16:03.587 --> 16:07.299
I realized too late that
you've been putting in so much effort.

16:08.175 --> 16:09.259
I'm sorry about back then.

16:09.843 --> 16:10.844
It's okay.

16:11.720 --> 16:13.889
Prejudice has also been my motivation.

16:14.807 --> 16:15.933
Wasn't it tough?

16:19.019 --> 16:22.189
Since we're in here,
I guess I should be honest.

16:23.357 --> 16:24.650
To be frank…

16:25.693 --> 16:28.278
I didn't always feel this way.

16:30.239 --> 16:33.867
At first, I wanted to prove
what kind of person I was

16:33.951 --> 16:35.077
to my mom.

17:09.236 --> 17:11.697
Every Sunday evening at eight,

17:11.780 --> 17:15.367
I'd call this number, on the dot.

17:15.451 --> 17:18.746
That was the only time I could be

17:18.829 --> 17:20.622
the top actress
Song Myeong-hwa's daughter.

17:22.541 --> 17:26.336
I bet I'll never be able
to forget this number.

17:27.880 --> 17:31.258
Then this number
became inactive five years ago?

17:33.719 --> 17:35.304
It was a long time before that.

17:35.971 --> 17:38.724
But how did this number become yours?

17:38.807 --> 17:40.350
That's a crazy coincidence.

17:50.778 --> 17:51.904
Ms. Dam.

17:53.155 --> 17:55.574
When I first answered your call,

17:56.909 --> 17:58.744
do you know why
I couldn't hang up right away?

18:02.039 --> 18:03.999
I could feel
the desperation in your voice.

18:08.128 --> 18:10.339
I'm not sure if it's my place to say this,

18:12.257 --> 18:13.592
but it seems like

18:14.718 --> 18:19.181
you truly miss your mother.

18:25.062 --> 18:27.106
-Perhaps now--
-That was just the meds talking.

18:29.233 --> 18:31.110
I can't have been sincere,

18:33.278 --> 18:36.031
because I don't even resent her anymore.

18:46.250 --> 18:48.502
It actually looks
pretty good on me, right?

18:50.170 --> 18:51.588
It fits well.

18:51.672 --> 18:54.091
And the belt can be about here.

18:54.675 --> 18:55.884
With the belt…

18:58.512 --> 19:01.056
Ye-jin was eager to do her best,

19:02.474 --> 19:04.518
because she'd be doing the broadcast
with you.

19:04.601 --> 19:05.602
Ye-jin

19:05.686 --> 19:07.896
isn't someone who'd do that.

19:09.481 --> 19:11.358
Think about it carefully, Myeong-hwa.

19:12.151 --> 19:16.989
You have to make sure
the pockets don't stick out…

19:20.659 --> 19:21.743
How is it?

19:21.827 --> 19:23.745
This is good.

19:24.746 --> 19:26.707
-All done, then.
-Okay.

19:46.768 --> 19:48.520
RAW MATERIAL SUPPLY CONTRACT

19:48.604 --> 19:50.272
GOJEUNEOK BIO
H.O. COSMETICS

19:50.355 --> 19:51.398
We appreciate this.

19:51.481 --> 19:54.276
The pleasure is ours.

19:54.776 --> 19:56.445
Mu-won, you're dressed nicely today.

19:56.528 --> 19:59.114
-Let's take a photo.
-We should.

19:59.198 --> 20:00.115
GOJEUNEOK BIO

20:00.199 --> 20:01.909
-Right here.
-Awesome.

20:02.659 --> 20:04.578
Hae-seok, come on.

20:04.661 --> 20:05.913
I'm fine. Take it without me.

20:06.830 --> 20:08.248
-Forget it, then.
-Fine.

20:10.500 --> 20:12.127
You really haven't changed at all.

20:13.962 --> 20:15.047
Right back at you.

20:17.257 --> 20:19.051
-All right, everyone.
-Mu-won,

20:20.302 --> 20:23.055
Hae-seok should be at the center.
What are you doing?

20:23.138 --> 20:25.474
-That's harsh.
-Is it? Move aside.

20:25.557 --> 20:27.100
That's right. Come on.

20:27.184 --> 20:28.143
Right here.

20:28.227 --> 20:30.103
This looks much nicer. Get in here.

20:30.187 --> 20:32.147
Smile. This is a great day.

20:32.231 --> 20:33.398
Whenever you're ready.

20:33.482 --> 20:35.317
One, two, three.

20:37.819 --> 20:38.820
Chang-ho.

20:38.904 --> 20:44.826
I almost cried reading the files
on H.O. Cosmetics.

20:44.910 --> 20:48.163
You must have started off
with nothing in Thailand.

20:48.956 --> 20:51.291
-It's amazing what you did.
-I thought the same

20:52.167 --> 20:55.045
whenever I heard about Gojeuneok Bio.

20:55.128 --> 20:58.257
You two were doing
an amazing job together.

20:58.340 --> 20:59.675
Chang-ho.

21:00.801 --> 21:02.386
You did a great job so far.

21:03.053 --> 21:04.471
You too.

21:06.431 --> 21:08.517
Why has Hae-seok become so quiet, though?

21:08.600 --> 21:10.352
He used to be really chatty.

21:10.435 --> 21:13.438
He's gotten much better
compared to before.

21:13.522 --> 21:14.731
This is a huge improvement.

21:15.232 --> 21:16.942
What… All right.

21:17.025 --> 21:18.318
He wants me to stop.

21:18.402 --> 21:20.529
I can read his eyes now.

21:21.613 --> 21:23.240
Hey, let's drink together.

21:23.323 --> 21:25.409
-Right. Come on.
-We should celebrate.

21:25.492 --> 21:26.702
-Goodness.
-Cheers!

21:31.415 --> 21:35.294
This reminds me of old times.

21:35.377 --> 21:37.671
The four of us always…

21:41.049 --> 21:42.968
I must be pretty drunk.

21:52.144 --> 21:53.145
Still,

21:54.271 --> 21:55.772
Woo-su did something right.

21:57.691 --> 21:58.817
What?

22:00.652 --> 22:02.112
He brought Hae-seok.

22:03.613 --> 22:04.781
Remember?

22:05.615 --> 22:06.616
He was making a fuss

22:06.700 --> 22:09.119
about getting a genius on board.

22:10.370 --> 22:12.247
How could I forget that?

22:37.397 --> 22:39.691
Hey, let's see where Hae-seok goes.

22:39.775 --> 22:43.695
He's the top of our class.
He'll join a major company for sure.

22:43.779 --> 22:44.905
Right?

22:44.988 --> 22:46.615
I'm jealous.

22:46.698 --> 22:49.159
RECRUITMENT FOR ENTRY-LEVEL POSITIONS

22:51.828 --> 22:53.997
WE DEVELOP COSMETICS
WITH FOOD-GRADE INGREDIENTS

22:56.124 --> 22:58.376
Nice to meet you. Come in.

23:00.629 --> 23:03.548
If they're food-grade cosmetics,
does it mean they're safe to eat?

23:04.508 --> 23:07.219
How can you make cosmetics
without chemical ingredients

23:07.302 --> 23:08.637
like parabens or silicones?

23:15.352 --> 23:17.354
What…

23:18.313 --> 23:21.650
I made these myself,
so I should be able to trust them.

23:23.276 --> 23:25.070
Would you like to try one?

23:33.787 --> 23:35.539
JOB APPLICATION SUBMISSION BOX

24:00.856 --> 24:01.815
I heard…

24:01.898 --> 24:02.732
APPLICATION FORM

24:02.816 --> 24:06.319
…major pharmaceutical companies
all wanted to recruit you.

24:08.155 --> 24:10.824
He said his hands were trembling
when he gave you the offer,

24:10.907 --> 24:13.118
and he was so grateful that you accepted.

24:13.201 --> 24:15.453
Woo-su said that whenever he got drunk.

24:18.832 --> 24:20.542
That jerk, Woo-su.

24:32.095 --> 24:33.096
You're back early.

24:52.490 --> 24:53.491
Just one minute.

24:56.244 --> 24:57.746
Let's stay like this for one minute.

25:00.207 --> 25:03.835
Hey. Did someone give you a hard time?

25:03.919 --> 25:06.379
Tell me. I can tear them down with words.

25:21.186 --> 25:22.187
Hang on.

25:23.104 --> 25:25.815
Mechoori, did you drink a lot today?

25:26.566 --> 25:27.943
Not at all.

25:28.568 --> 25:30.654
Be careful.

25:33.406 --> 25:36.034
Get some rest.
I'll bring you something to drink.

25:39.955 --> 25:41.831
Are you going to keep calling me Mechoori?

25:42.582 --> 25:43.667
What else would I call you?

25:44.751 --> 25:46.753
Well, you know…

25:47.712 --> 25:48.713
What?

25:49.756 --> 25:50.882
I mean…

25:51.883 --> 25:53.301
there are a lot of options.

25:54.469 --> 25:56.429
I have no idea.

25:59.099 --> 26:00.850
Matthew.

26:03.353 --> 26:04.604
But

26:04.688 --> 26:07.691
why do you want to be called Matthew
when you have a pretty name?

26:08.400 --> 26:10.485
Did you use that name abroad?

26:15.198 --> 26:17.117
Som-yi made it for me.

26:35.677 --> 26:39.097
You're really here.

26:39.723 --> 26:42.058
Why are you hiding here?

26:42.142 --> 26:44.019
Are you playing hide-and-seek?

26:57.741 --> 26:58.825
I found you.

27:00.493 --> 27:03.288
Aren't you cold?

27:04.456 --> 27:06.416
Here, drink this.

27:25.518 --> 27:27.771
Everyone says you're stupid.

27:27.854 --> 27:29.856
They say you can't talk.

27:30.648 --> 27:31.941
There's nothing wrong with that.

27:53.671 --> 27:54.506
MATTHEW AND FRIENDS

27:54.589 --> 27:55.882
Do you want to read this?

27:55.965 --> 27:58.301
This is my favorite book.

27:58.927 --> 28:02.222
There aren't any words written in it,

28:02.847 --> 28:05.517
but you can understand everything.

28:12.190 --> 28:14.609
Can you really not talk?

28:16.277 --> 28:19.155
If I tell you a secret first,

28:19.239 --> 28:21.324
will you tell me one too?

28:22.367 --> 28:24.536
I won't tell anyone.

28:24.619 --> 28:27.205
I don't have any friends anyway.

28:32.127 --> 28:33.336
Because of this.

28:41.761 --> 28:44.556
Don't you have any secrets?

28:47.517 --> 28:48.685
That's not fair.

28:49.811 --> 28:51.688
What's your name?

28:53.690 --> 28:55.525
Did you forget?

28:56.526 --> 28:59.154
Then should I give you a name?

29:03.742 --> 29:05.160
Matthew.

29:05.827 --> 29:08.496
What do you think, Uncle Matthew?

29:13.960 --> 29:15.754
If it weren't for Som-yi back then,

29:17.380 --> 29:19.841
I wouldn't have been able to do anything.

29:21.426 --> 29:23.136
I shamelessly…

29:24.304 --> 29:29.267
received comfort from that little kid.

29:36.065 --> 29:42.071
You know how much Som-yi likes you, right?

29:47.952 --> 29:50.288
That's why I have to pay her back
for the rest of my life.

29:51.164 --> 29:52.165
No,

29:53.708 --> 29:55.084
I will make it up to her.

30:08.056 --> 30:12.143
Second block past the intersection,
below the red sign.

30:12.227 --> 30:14.020
All the signs are red.

30:39.087 --> 30:41.172
-Are they flashers or something?
-Maybe.

30:41.256 --> 30:42.966
He's handsome.

30:43.049 --> 30:44.634
They look suspicious.

30:45.802 --> 30:47.679
I got some info.

30:47.762 --> 30:48.847
What is it?

30:48.930 --> 30:51.474
Gojeuneok Bio rejected
Ms. Michelle's offer

30:52.225 --> 30:54.811
and signed a contract with a company
called H.O. Cosmetics.

30:58.648 --> 31:00.567
Michelle must be really pissed.

31:00.650 --> 31:01.776
That's right.

31:01.860 --> 31:03.862
But she's not the type to sit still.

31:04.779 --> 31:07.282
So I was really anxious
about how she'd react, but…

31:07.365 --> 31:08.449
But?

31:09.492 --> 31:10.743
She's just sitting still.

31:12.996 --> 31:14.956
But I'm sure she's up to something.

31:15.498 --> 31:17.333
She hasn't been sharing info with me,

31:17.417 --> 31:20.169
and she's been handling schedules
on her own.

31:50.533 --> 31:51.367
What?

31:52.577 --> 31:55.496
Did my looks leave you speechless?

31:56.164 --> 31:57.040
You're beautiful.

31:59.751 --> 32:00.960
Did you have something to say?

32:01.961 --> 32:05.214
Do you have a broadcast tomorrow?

32:05.924 --> 32:07.467
No, why?

32:08.217 --> 32:09.594
How about a hotel vacation?

32:10.803 --> 32:11.638
What?

32:11.721 --> 32:13.890
A hotel vacation with Mr. Proper?

32:15.350 --> 32:17.393
Thanks for announcing it to everyone.

32:17.477 --> 32:20.396
I'm just jealous, that's all.
That's awesome.

32:20.480 --> 32:23.816
What would you be jealous about?
It's nothing special.

32:23.900 --> 32:25.526
Have you prepared everything?

32:26.319 --> 32:29.072
What do you mean? Prepare what?

32:29.155 --> 32:33.034
A hotel vacation isn't a real vacation.
It's a hardcore training session.

32:33.117 --> 32:36.579
You need a swimsuit, a dinner outfit,
a gym outfit, and loungewear.

32:36.663 --> 32:38.790
Prepare everything perfectly,
or you'll regret it.

32:38.873 --> 32:40.792
It's a battlefield, understand?

32:40.875 --> 32:42.168
-You should stop eating.
-What…

32:42.669 --> 32:43.544
Don't be silly.

32:44.212 --> 32:45.254
It's fine.

32:49.258 --> 32:50.927
Why are you blushing?

32:51.010 --> 32:52.220
-What?
-What are you thinking?

32:52.303 --> 32:53.513
It's nothing.

33:07.193 --> 33:08.194
Today's workout complete.

33:08.277 --> 33:10.113
TWC: COMMONLY USED FITNESS HASHTAG

33:12.198 --> 33:13.700
I need some sugar after that workout.

33:23.042 --> 33:27.505
This has a lot of protein but no flour.
It's pretty impressive.

33:28.589 --> 33:29.757
Just like you.

33:30.800 --> 33:32.343
Do you want one? It's tasty.

33:36.806 --> 33:38.474
There's a variety of flavors.

33:45.148 --> 33:46.482
I like the cheese flavor.

33:48.568 --> 33:50.028
Why are you carrying so many?

34:05.668 --> 34:07.503
Why are you so busy?

34:07.587 --> 34:09.130
I'm out of the office tomorrow.

34:09.213 --> 34:11.340
Oh, right.
You're taking the day off tomorrow.

34:11.424 --> 34:13.342
Are things busy at the farm?
Should I help out?

34:13.426 --> 34:15.219
No, it's fine.

34:23.853 --> 34:25.229
Sung-mi's so silly.

34:25.813 --> 34:27.899
Preparing for a hotel vacation?
That's tacky.

34:27.982 --> 34:29.567
It's not like it's my first time.

34:36.824 --> 34:39.368
Right. It's our official first date.

34:41.496 --> 34:43.456
This is just a matter of etiquette.

34:46.459 --> 34:48.294
I feel like there's something missing.

34:51.464 --> 34:53.257
You're Dam Ye-jin, right?

34:53.758 --> 34:54.884
I'm a huge fan.

34:54.967 --> 34:56.052
You're so beautiful.

34:56.135 --> 34:57.929
Thank you.

34:58.429 --> 35:00.348
Are you buying a gift?

35:00.431 --> 35:01.974
Or is it for yourself?

35:02.058 --> 35:03.059
It's for myself.

35:03.142 --> 35:04.352
But I'd like something

35:04.435 --> 35:07.688
that won't seem like
I've been excited for this day,

35:07.772 --> 35:11.192
or like I want to stand out too much,

35:11.275 --> 35:13.361
but still charm a guy.

35:13.444 --> 35:14.862
Is there a necklace like that?

35:14.946 --> 35:16.114
Then how about this?

35:20.326 --> 35:21.577
I'll take this one.

35:29.710 --> 35:31.420
Why do you have so much luggage?

35:31.504 --> 35:32.880
Women always have lots of luggage.

35:48.271 --> 35:49.981
Are you feeling uncomfortable
or something?

35:53.568 --> 35:54.402
Let's go.

35:56.779 --> 35:58.281
That necklace looks great on you.

36:00.950 --> 36:02.410
Don't get the wrong idea.

36:02.493 --> 36:04.620
I didn't buy it
just for our hotel vacation.

36:04.704 --> 36:08.749
I just believe that fashion
is about the finishing touch,

36:08.833 --> 36:11.627
so I bought it to complete my look today.

36:17.341 --> 36:19.260
Welcome.

36:19.343 --> 36:20.636
May I have your name, please?

36:20.720 --> 36:23.014
Matthew… I mean, Lee Hae-seok.

36:23.097 --> 36:24.599
Just a moment, sir.

36:26.893 --> 36:28.644
It's confirmed.

36:28.728 --> 36:30.479
Room 507, sir.

36:30.563 --> 36:32.899
Scan the key card in the elevator

36:32.982 --> 36:34.567
and select your floor.

36:35.151 --> 36:36.777
And Room 508, sir.

36:36.861 --> 36:38.029
Right.

36:38.613 --> 36:40.323
-And this is Room 509.
-Right.

36:41.073 --> 36:42.700
And Room 510.

36:42.783 --> 36:44.160
Right. Thank you.

36:48.331 --> 36:49.498
That's all, ma'am.

36:50.333 --> 36:51.584
That should be all.

36:53.002 --> 36:55.129
Why did you book so many rooms?

36:55.213 --> 36:57.423
Is early check-in available?

36:57.506 --> 37:00.134
Early check-in!

37:01.594 --> 37:03.095
Ms. Dam!

37:03.179 --> 37:04.388
Sweetie!

37:04.972 --> 37:06.182
-Mechoori!
-Hi!

37:06.933 --> 37:07.767
Coach!

37:07.850 --> 37:09.018
Som-yi.

37:09.101 --> 37:10.603
This is truly a great item.

37:10.686 --> 37:11.896
We're here.

37:14.398 --> 37:16.943
What's going on?

37:17.026 --> 37:18.611
You said we're having a hotel vacation.

37:18.694 --> 37:19.820
Yes,

37:19.904 --> 37:20.988
with the other villagers.

37:23.157 --> 37:24.700
I told you last time

37:24.784 --> 37:26.535
that I booked rooms for everyone.

37:29.747 --> 37:32.750
Right. You said that.

37:33.793 --> 37:35.211
How have you been?

37:35.294 --> 37:36.420
Sweetie!

37:36.504 --> 37:37.672
It's nice seeing you here.

37:37.755 --> 37:39.715
I finished the check-in. Let's go.

37:39.799 --> 37:41.300
What?

37:41.384 --> 37:42.843
-Off to our rooms already?
-No way.

37:42.927 --> 37:44.303
-There's so much to see.
-No.

37:44.387 --> 37:47.473
We came all the way here.
We have to at least look around.

37:47.556 --> 37:50.601
I bet they have all sorts of stuff here.

37:50.685 --> 37:54.146
Is your workplace far from here?

37:54.230 --> 37:56.399
Can you show us around?

37:58.067 --> 37:59.360
HIT Homeshopping?

37:59.443 --> 38:01.988
-Coach, we want a tour too.
-Gosh.

38:02.071 --> 38:04.156
-Let's go.
-Right now?

38:04.240 --> 38:07.994
My wife wore what she used to wear
when she was single for it.

38:08.077 --> 38:10.079
Ms. Dam doesn't have a broadcast today,

38:10.162 --> 38:11.455
so that's going to be difficult.

38:11.539 --> 38:12.456
What?

38:12.540 --> 38:14.250
-We can't go?
-No way.

38:14.333 --> 38:18.087
We came here to see
the home shopping headquarters.

38:18.170 --> 38:19.213
We have to see it.

38:19.297 --> 38:20.715
This is bad.

38:25.970 --> 38:27.596
Mr. Hwang.

38:27.680 --> 38:30.182
Are there any goblin filler shows
I can step in for today?

38:30.266 --> 38:31.767
GOBLIN: A FILLER BROADCAST

38:32.601 --> 38:33.436
I'll do it.

38:33.978 --> 38:36.022
HIT HOMESHOPPING'S EXCLUSIVE HOST
DAM YE-JIN

38:37.356 --> 38:38.858
Isn't that Ye-jin?

38:39.567 --> 38:41.152
You look completely different…

38:41.235 --> 38:43.279
-Is she prettier than me?
-Of course she is.

38:43.362 --> 38:44.238
She isn't human.

38:45.698 --> 38:48.326
-She looks like an angel.
-She's a total angel.

38:48.826 --> 38:50.578
An angel sent from heaven.

38:51.579 --> 38:52.747
She's beautiful.

38:52.830 --> 38:54.332
-Jin-yi.
-Yes?

38:55.041 --> 38:55.958
Jin-yi.

38:56.042 --> 38:58.294
Look, that's what I showed you last time.

38:58.377 --> 38:59.879
OPEN RECRUITMENT FOR NEW HOSTS

38:59.962 --> 39:01.630
All right, everyone. Let's head inside.

39:01.714 --> 39:03.758
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

39:03.841 --> 39:04.842
She looks so different.

39:07.386 --> 39:08.387
Let's go.

39:08.471 --> 39:09.847
Did you apply?

39:09.930 --> 39:11.807
Why would I apply?

39:12.516 --> 39:13.684
Sorry.

39:15.269 --> 39:16.354
Thank you.

39:20.691 --> 39:21.901
You're from Deokpung, right?

39:22.735 --> 39:24.111
-Yes.
-It's you, right?

39:24.195 --> 39:25.613
Thank you.

39:31.118 --> 39:32.620
Are you here to apply for a position?

39:32.703 --> 39:34.705
-I…
-That's great.

39:35.498 --> 39:36.582
I'll see you later, then.

39:37.708 --> 39:40.544
Oh, and my name's Ki-hong.

39:42.213 --> 39:43.714
Ki-hong…

39:58.938 --> 40:00.356
What do you think?

40:01.190 --> 40:03.776
It's great! Thank you.

40:07.613 --> 40:08.948
Ms. Dam.

40:09.031 --> 40:09.949
Yes?

40:12.576 --> 40:13.577
What is it?

40:13.661 --> 40:15.121
This was a last-minute broadcast,

40:15.204 --> 40:17.748
so there was only one model
who could make it.

40:18.457 --> 40:20.501
The screen might seem a bit empty…

40:24.255 --> 40:26.966
Let me introduce

40:27.049 --> 40:29.760
Sollen's steady collection
of men's jackets.

40:32.680 --> 40:36.934
Every jacket in this collection
is wrinkle-resistant.

40:37.476 --> 40:38.853
He looks cool.

40:40.271 --> 40:43.315
And they're made
with breathable, 3D-structured fabric,

40:43.399 --> 40:46.777
so even those who run hot can stay cool.

40:47.570 --> 40:50.698
The fabric is machine-washable,
so they're easy to care for.

40:51.323 --> 40:53.492
They even offer UV protection.

40:53.576 --> 40:55.995
All these features are contained
in these jackets.

40:57.163 --> 41:00.332
Thanks to your incredible response,

41:00.416 --> 41:03.627
the brown option you're seeing now
is already sold out.

41:04.712 --> 41:06.130
For real? He's not even a model.

41:06.213 --> 41:08.966
-Why?
-I had no expectations at all.

41:09.049 --> 41:10.926
What's great about Sollen's jackets

41:11.010 --> 41:13.262
is that the waist isn't overly tapered.

41:13.345 --> 41:14.847
So if you look here,

41:15.431 --> 41:19.768
the fit stays perfectly intact
even when it's buttoned up,

41:19.852 --> 41:22.605
and there is still plenty of room
for comfort.

41:26.734 --> 41:29.320
What is he doing? Geez.

41:30.112 --> 41:31.363
Mr. Park is so cool.

41:32.448 --> 41:33.491
I'm not so sure.

41:33.991 --> 41:35.493
I'd like to buy one.

41:36.076 --> 41:38.120
Can you order one for me?

41:39.163 --> 41:41.248
-I'll use my account.
-Okay.

41:42.124 --> 41:43.375
WHO'S THAT MODEL?

41:44.001 --> 41:45.127
He's so cute.

41:49.798 --> 41:51.383
Let's run both stills here,

41:51.467 --> 41:53.636
then cut to highlights three and five.

41:53.719 --> 41:54.845
Three and five.

41:56.597 --> 41:58.265
How adorable.

42:01.268 --> 42:02.144
Mr. Park!

42:03.270 --> 42:04.313
Ms. Eom!

42:05.481 --> 42:07.191
This is a gift for you.

42:07.274 --> 42:08.901
The jacket suited you so well.

42:08.984 --> 42:11.946
Come on. I didn't do anything.

42:12.530 --> 42:14.031
Oh, and…

42:14.114 --> 42:15.282
I bought some

42:15.866 --> 42:17.284
today as well.

42:19.620 --> 42:20.829
But

42:20.913 --> 42:24.625
are you sure you're buying all this
because you need it?

42:24.708 --> 42:27.002
I bought them because you're selling them.

42:27.086 --> 42:28.796
I never asked you to buy anything.

42:28.879 --> 42:30.130
Why would you go that far?

42:30.214 --> 42:31.882
Do you know how much all that costs?

42:32.633 --> 42:34.218
I was just…

42:37.137 --> 42:40.933
I wanted a reason
to send you a text, Ms. Eom.

42:42.226 --> 42:45.854
Plus, it didn't really cost me that much.

42:45.938 --> 42:49.900
Seeing you smile once is enough for me.

42:53.153 --> 42:56.657
Then you must have bought
the hotel vacation package too.

42:56.740 --> 42:57.700
Of course.

42:59.535 --> 43:01.412
Should we go together, then?

43:15.843 --> 43:17.219
Are you going somewhere?

43:17.303 --> 43:18.679
I'm making a delivery.

43:19.179 --> 43:20.472
Can I join you?

43:23.142 --> 43:24.143
Dressed like that?

43:27.229 --> 43:28.522
What's wrong with this outfit?

43:30.608 --> 43:32.026
You'd better not regret it, then.

43:49.376 --> 43:50.794
We should be there soon.

43:54.173 --> 43:55.382
We're here.

43:55.466 --> 43:56.842
That's a relief.

44:02.806 --> 44:03.724
The coffee's fine.

44:03.807 --> 44:05.768
-Be careful.
-It's fine.

44:07.144 --> 44:09.313
Ma'am, sir.

44:09.396 --> 44:11.357
Come and have your coffee.

44:11.440 --> 44:13.317
Hey, Ae-ra.

44:14.026 --> 44:15.194
What is it?

44:16.987 --> 44:17.988
Is something wrong?

44:19.073 --> 44:22.284
My husband had a little accident in bed.

44:22.368 --> 44:25.412
I was trying to wash him,
but I can hardly even move him.

44:26.497 --> 44:27.581
All right.

44:28.832 --> 44:29.667
I'll go.

44:33.671 --> 44:35.089
Sir, hello.

44:36.215 --> 44:37.716
You must be feeling uncomfortable.

44:37.800 --> 44:40.260
Let me help you to the bathroom.

44:41.345 --> 44:42.179
Oh, dear.

44:42.262 --> 44:45.057
Ma'am, could I use this cloth
next to the sheets?

44:45.140 --> 44:47.351
-Sure.
-Thank you.

44:51.480 --> 44:53.816
Ma'am, where's the bathroom?

44:53.899 --> 44:55.025
Over there.

44:55.109 --> 44:56.276
Thank you.

44:57.569 --> 44:59.488
Your clothes seem expensive.
You'll ruin them.

44:59.571 --> 45:01.949
-Oh, dear.
-It's completely fine.

45:11.125 --> 45:13.544
The blood pressure pills
have to be taken every morning.

45:14.420 --> 45:17.214
I'll pick you up at 10:00 a.m.
on the physical therapy days.

45:17.840 --> 45:18.841
All right?

45:45.784 --> 45:48.704
I hope she doesn't forget the meds.

46:01.800 --> 46:03.177
I should get him a new shirt.

46:03.886 --> 46:06.930
No, I should just get them full outfits.

46:07.014 --> 46:09.099
Ms. Moon, do you know their shoe sizes?

46:11.101 --> 46:12.144
Just get them anything.

46:12.978 --> 46:14.563
I'm Kang Mu-won.

46:15.147 --> 46:16.523
I don't half-ass anything.

46:18.275 --> 46:20.777
Where did you keep your watch?

46:22.237 --> 46:23.238
I got rid of it.

46:23.322 --> 46:24.531
What?

46:24.615 --> 46:27.034
You threw away that expensive watch?

46:27.659 --> 46:29.161
It didn't seem to be your style.

46:31.455 --> 46:33.582
But I guess you know
a thing or two about watches.

46:34.791 --> 46:36.585
No, I have no clue.

46:37.920 --> 46:39.796
It's just that it was the same one

46:39.880 --> 46:41.882
that someone really annoying used to wear.

46:55.896 --> 46:57.397
Why are you following me?

46:57.481 --> 47:00.400
You booked a vacation with your villagers.
You should be with them.

47:01.318 --> 47:02.236
Are you angry?

47:03.070 --> 47:04.446
No.

47:04.530 --> 47:05.906
Thank you

47:05.989 --> 47:10.244
for using my hotel vacation package
in such a meaningful way, sir.

47:10.327 --> 47:11.286
I…

47:12.412 --> 47:14.248
You seem mistaken about something.

47:19.127 --> 47:21.255
Our date is just starting now.

47:23.215 --> 47:25.217
-What?
-It's starting now.

47:29.763 --> 47:30.931
What's going on?

48:01.920 --> 48:04.381
-Isn't it tasty?
-It is.

48:27.696 --> 48:30.616
-That's hot!
-You just gulped it down…

48:52.763 --> 48:55.098
Mechoori, look at this.

48:56.350 --> 48:57.726
This line.

49:37.933 --> 49:39.142
Do you feel better now?

49:39.226 --> 49:40.060
What do you mean?

49:40.143 --> 49:41.728
You were sulking earlier.

49:42.729 --> 49:44.106
I wasn't sulking.

49:44.690 --> 49:47.150
You were pouting like this.

49:47.776 --> 49:49.319
Don't tease me.

49:55.909 --> 49:59.329
I think I'll take the elders home
and sleep at home in Deokpung tomorrow.

49:59.413 --> 50:01.164
Really?

50:02.124 --> 50:03.375
But there's Mr. Park too.

50:04.668 --> 50:06.169
I just want to do it.

50:07.754 --> 50:10.382
Why are you always trying
to take care of everything by yourself?

50:11.216 --> 50:14.094
Are your shoulders wide
because of all the weight you carry?

50:16.096 --> 50:18.640
I wasn't joking. I mean it.

50:19.391 --> 50:21.017
You should put down some of that burden.

50:21.101 --> 50:23.770
You should live for yourself as well.

50:30.277 --> 50:33.697
Have you thought about
developing cosmetics again?

50:39.661 --> 50:41.413
That photo I saw last time…

50:43.790 --> 50:45.125
It was my first time

50:45.208 --> 50:46.835
seeing you with such a bright smile.

50:49.254 --> 50:52.924
I'll do anything I can
to see you smile like that again,

50:53.508 --> 50:55.385
just like you did for me.

50:56.219 --> 50:57.929
So think about it.

50:58.638 --> 50:59.473
Okay?

51:02.392 --> 51:03.226
Hey!

51:04.478 --> 51:06.813
You always give firm answers,
but you're not saying no.

51:10.108 --> 51:11.234
I'll stop here today.

51:16.656 --> 51:21.036
You can always place your concerns
or burdens on my shoulder.

51:21.828 --> 51:24.039
I'm pretty strong, you know.

51:26.583 --> 51:27.584
Thank you.

51:54.361 --> 51:55.612
Did you get it?

51:55.695 --> 51:58.323
Ms. Michelle, this is urgent.

51:58.865 --> 52:00.575
The car…

52:00.659 --> 52:02.953
-What about the car?
-The car…

52:03.036 --> 52:07.123
Oh, gosh! You have to hurry.
You need to come, right now.

52:07.791 --> 52:10.210
-It's cold in the parking lot.
-Hurry.

52:10.293 --> 52:12.295
-Hurry!
-What is it?

52:27.978 --> 52:28.854
Hurry. Come on.

52:28.937 --> 52:30.397
This is a disaster.

52:30.480 --> 52:31.773
What do I do?

52:32.607 --> 52:33.567
What is it?

52:40.198 --> 52:44.828
I drove really carefully,
keeping to 60 kilometers per hour.

52:44.911 --> 52:48.331
But when I parked here, it was like this.

52:53.920 --> 52:57.841
I really wanted to get you a sandwich

52:57.924 --> 53:00.468
with freshly picked arugula!

53:01.678 --> 53:03.263
So you're saying

53:03.346 --> 53:06.224
this huge emergency

53:07.058 --> 53:08.977
was that this sandwich

53:09.936 --> 53:11.563
became a huge mess?

53:13.732 --> 53:15.025
That's right, ma'am.

53:15.817 --> 53:17.652
Your lunch

53:17.736 --> 53:21.740
is fuel to run our entire brand.

53:23.408 --> 53:24.659
-Mr. Cha.
-Yes, ma'am.

53:25.619 --> 53:27.078
What's with you?

53:28.872 --> 53:29.873
What's wrong with you?

53:31.124 --> 53:33.251
That's why I reserved a restaurant nearby.

53:33.335 --> 53:34.336
Let's head there.

53:34.419 --> 53:36.421
I don't want any of it!

53:40.133 --> 53:41.968
Then I'll go and make…

53:42.052 --> 53:42.928
You idiot!

53:43.011 --> 53:44.512
-I'll make one--
-You idiot!

53:44.596 --> 53:46.932
You can't head back now…

53:53.980 --> 53:56.358
If you waste my time like this
one more time,

53:57.150 --> 53:59.402
you're out. I mean it.

54:00.654 --> 54:01.821
Sorry, ma'am.

54:07.202 --> 54:09.287
Go and get me some hot coffee.

54:09.371 --> 54:10.330
Yes, ma'am.

54:19.172 --> 54:20.340
The first sip has to be cool.

54:20.423 --> 54:21.633
Yes, ma'am.

54:21.716 --> 54:25.053
A hot coffee with a cool first sip…
Is that possible?

54:25.136 --> 54:27.555
I'll go get one straight away.

54:44.447 --> 54:45.448
DEOKPUNG COMMUNITY CENTER

54:45.532 --> 54:46.700
Right, let's go!

54:48.660 --> 54:49.744
Let's get a move on.

54:50.620 --> 54:52.330
Mechoori.

54:52.414 --> 54:56.209
I had an incredible time thanks to you.

54:58.294 --> 55:01.548
Do something about those two, will you?

55:01.631 --> 55:02.757
See you.

55:03.591 --> 55:04.676
-Bye.
-Bye.

55:07.762 --> 55:08.722
Thanks.

55:14.686 --> 55:16.187
-Let's go.
-No!

55:16.271 --> 55:17.480
I don't want to live with you.

55:18.440 --> 55:19.774
Na Som-yi.

55:20.316 --> 55:22.652
I'm going to live with Mechoori now.

55:22.736 --> 55:23.611
Hurry up.

55:25.739 --> 55:27.198
Fine, do whatever you want.

56:26.508 --> 56:28.259
Did you get in another fight with Jin-yi?

56:28.343 --> 56:29.594
What happened?

56:30.428 --> 56:34.099
I just feel so upset, Mechoori.

56:34.766 --> 56:36.768
She told me

56:36.851 --> 56:39.437
not to eat anything at the buffet.

56:40.688 --> 56:42.899
We went all the way to Seoul,

56:43.525 --> 56:47.654
but she wouldn't let me have
a single bite.

56:59.207 --> 57:02.085
SOM'S VARIETY SHOP

57:03.586 --> 57:04.796
Jin-yi.

57:05.964 --> 57:08.299
Som-yi's asleep. I'll go put her to bed.

57:26.860 --> 57:28.236
This is our last rent.

57:28.319 --> 57:29.195
Your last rent?

57:29.904 --> 57:31.239
I'm going to Seoul with Som-yi.

57:32.282 --> 57:33.199
Why? That's so sudden.

57:33.283 --> 57:34.159
It's not.

57:34.242 --> 57:35.994
I've been thinking about it for some time.

57:37.328 --> 57:40.665
The doctor recommended
taking Som-yi to a bigger hospital,

57:40.748 --> 57:42.083
but it's in Seoul.

57:43.126 --> 57:44.502
It's too far to go back and forth.

57:44.586 --> 57:46.379
I can take her back and forth.

57:46.463 --> 57:47.630
No, don't say that.

57:47.714 --> 57:50.091
You know how much Som-yi loves this place.

57:51.050 --> 57:53.136
She's getting along well at school now.

57:54.888 --> 57:56.931
That's why I want to hurry.

57:57.599 --> 57:59.601
She'll leave with happy memories.

58:00.643 --> 58:03.104
No matter how much I think about it,
this is the right choice.

58:03.938 --> 58:05.732
We should leave
before she learns everything.

58:08.276 --> 58:11.362
If that's the reason,
then I should be the one leaving.

58:13.072 --> 58:14.741
I'll explain it to Som-yi.

58:14.824 --> 58:16.284
What will you tell her?

58:16.951 --> 58:19.704
That what happened to her
was because of the cream you made?

58:19.787 --> 58:21.831
She has to know sooner or later.

58:21.915 --> 58:24.083
-She's better off not knowing--
-Jin-yi.

58:25.210 --> 58:26.503
We'll discuss this later.

58:48.358 --> 58:49.234
Jin-yi.

58:49.317 --> 58:51.027
What do I do?

58:51.110 --> 58:52.320
Som-yi's missing.

58:53.613 --> 58:54.447
What?

58:54.531 --> 58:56.074
She was asleep,

58:56.157 --> 58:58.076
so I just went to work,
but she disappeared.

58:58.159 --> 59:00.161
What do I do? Her phone's off, too.

59:00.245 --> 59:01.829
She must've heard us earlier.

59:01.913 --> 59:02.872
What do I do?

59:04.249 --> 59:05.708
I'll head over there.

59:05.792 --> 59:08.878
Attention, residents of Deokpung Village.

59:08.962 --> 59:14.175
Som-yi hasn't come home,
and is not answering her phone.

59:14.259 --> 59:17.011
If anyone is with her or has seen her,

59:17.095 --> 59:20.348
please contact Som's Variety Shop.

59:20.431 --> 59:23.851
-Som-yi!
-Som-yi!

59:23.935 --> 59:26.020
-Did you find her?
-No.

59:26.104 --> 59:27.897
-Let's go that way.
-Okay.

59:27.981 --> 59:29.107
-Som-yi!
-What do we do?

59:29.190 --> 59:31.192
-Som-yi!
-Som-yi!

59:31.276 --> 59:32.151
Where has she gone?

59:32.235 --> 59:34.153
-Som-yi!
-Som-yi!

59:34.237 --> 59:36.322
-Na Som-yi!
-Na Som-yi!

59:38.491 --> 59:40.118
-Na Som-yi!
-Na Som-yi!

59:40.201 --> 59:42.078
-Jin-yi, check over there.
-Okay.

59:42.579 --> 59:44.122
Na Som-yi!

59:44.205 --> 59:45.290
Som-yi!

59:47.542 --> 59:48.543
Na Som-yi!

01:00:19.032 --> 01:00:20.283
Som-yi.

01:00:21.034 --> 01:00:22.160
Mechoori.

01:00:22.243 --> 01:00:23.494
Are you okay?

01:00:26.914 --> 01:00:28.583
To be honest…

01:00:29.250 --> 01:00:31.169
I already knew everything.

01:00:36.341 --> 01:00:37.342
Som-yi.

01:00:39.469 --> 01:00:41.512
I'm so sorry.

01:00:42.930 --> 01:00:44.223
I'm…

01:00:45.183 --> 01:00:46.643
really sorry.

01:00:46.726 --> 01:00:48.519
I already know.

01:00:48.603 --> 01:00:50.772
You apologized every day.

01:00:50.855 --> 01:00:53.399
You brought me gifts
every time you went to Seoul,

01:00:53.483 --> 01:00:57.362
you cooked for me, cut fruit for me,

01:00:57.445 --> 01:00:59.197
and even attended my school field day.

01:01:01.407 --> 01:01:04.619
Are you going to leave?

01:01:05.244 --> 01:01:07.622
You told Jin-yi earlier

01:01:07.705 --> 01:01:09.415
that you'd leave.

01:01:11.542 --> 01:01:15.505
Are you going to abandon us
like Mom and Dad did?

01:01:19.342 --> 01:01:21.219
It's not like that, Som-yi.

01:01:22.720 --> 01:01:24.639
I'm going to protect you

01:01:26.057 --> 01:01:28.893
until you go to college,
find what you want to do,

01:01:32.689 --> 01:01:34.649
achieve your dream,

01:01:36.317 --> 01:01:37.902
and get all better.

01:01:40.738 --> 01:01:42.782
You'd better keep that promise.

01:01:44.409 --> 01:01:45.410
Of course.

01:01:46.369 --> 01:01:48.371
Promise me.

01:01:52.709 --> 01:01:54.001
I promise.

01:02:07.807 --> 01:02:11.185
Jin-yi, Mechoori's going to find her.

01:02:12.395 --> 01:02:14.230
She'll be fine.

01:02:14.313 --> 01:02:15.398
Don't worry.

01:02:16.190 --> 01:02:18.609
It's all my fault.

01:02:18.693 --> 01:02:21.988
I shouldn't have brought Som-yi here.

01:02:22.071 --> 01:02:23.698
Don't cry.

01:02:23.781 --> 01:02:26.492
The bruises you make
in your own heart won't heal.

01:02:26.576 --> 01:02:28.035
Don't cry.

01:02:28.911 --> 01:02:30.455
Jin-yi.

01:02:41.090 --> 01:02:42.675
I'm sorry, Jin-yi.

01:02:42.759 --> 01:02:45.261
No, I'm sorry.

01:02:45.344 --> 01:02:47.388
I'm sorry, Som-yi.

01:02:49.599 --> 01:02:51.058
Jin-yi.

01:02:52.101 --> 01:02:54.937
Can't we keep living here?

01:02:55.646 --> 01:02:58.983
I want to stay here.

01:03:00.902 --> 01:03:03.571
All right. Let's stay.

01:03:54.497 --> 01:03:55.331
You did it.

01:03:56.791 --> 01:03:58.292
Mr. Cha!

01:04:01.629 --> 01:04:04.966
Do you know anything
about the Asian market entry plans?

01:04:05.049 --> 01:04:06.926
Asian market entry?

01:04:08.010 --> 01:04:09.595
What are you talking about?

01:04:09.679 --> 01:04:11.389
We can't even find
raw materials right now.

01:04:11.889 --> 01:04:13.683
What… How?

01:04:15.101 --> 01:04:16.477
That's what I want to ask.

01:04:16.978 --> 01:04:19.856
What on earth is she thinking right now?

01:04:22.316 --> 01:04:25.653
It will be quite different
once we start developing properly.

01:04:26.279 --> 01:04:28.239
We'll have various devices here.

01:04:30.116 --> 01:04:32.159
Develop what?

01:04:33.578 --> 01:04:36.330
I'm going to start
developing cosmetics again.

01:04:37.415 --> 01:04:38.416
Mechoori.

01:04:40.209 --> 01:04:42.169
I made a promise to Som-yi.

01:04:42.795 --> 01:04:46.007
I'm going to make
the perfect cream this time.

01:04:48.342 --> 01:04:49.635
I won't leave any regrets.

01:05:20.291 --> 01:05:22.960
Thank you for coming.

01:05:23.836 --> 01:05:25.046
I was curious

01:05:25.129 --> 01:05:28.215
what you meant by helping me

01:05:28.716 --> 01:05:29.884
get rid of a nuisance.

01:05:32.678 --> 01:05:34.221
Gojeuneok Bio.

01:05:35.389 --> 01:05:39.518
I'll wrap it up nicely
and deliver it to you.

01:05:57.078 --> 01:05:59.956
SOLD OUT ON YOU

01:06:00.039 --> 01:06:05.962
THANKS TO SPECIAL GUEST SEO HYUN-WOO

01:06:33.072 --> 01:06:34.782
Why didn't you come that day?

01:06:36.075 --> 01:06:38.244
-Go and sleep.
-I'm going to sleep here.

01:06:39.745 --> 01:06:43.040
Gojeuneok Bio's first cosmetic product
will be a regenerative cream.

01:06:43.124 --> 01:06:44.125
I made this cream.

01:06:44.208 --> 01:06:45.668
What should I name it?

01:06:45.751 --> 01:06:47.086
Noori Cream.

01:06:47.169 --> 01:06:49.839
I brought my first item
for Dam Ye-jin's Only1.

01:06:49.922 --> 01:06:53.426
The Noori Cream is the hottest item
among the merchandisers right now.

01:06:54.051 --> 01:06:55.094
Are you that happy?

01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:58.681
I'm going to make sure Lee Hae-seok
can never set foot in this industry again.

01:06:58.764 --> 01:06:59.598
Mechoori.

01:06:59.682 --> 01:07:02.560
A bunch of people stormed in
and made a total mess in the village.

01:07:02.643 --> 01:07:04.854
I'll leave the village

01:07:04.937 --> 01:07:06.230
before I cause any more trouble.

01:07:12.945 --> 01:07:14.947
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
